The following material is derived from that project (Apache-2.0):

- src/assets/rule-docs.ts — the complete built-in per-language review
  ruleset (54 rule documents) and its file-pattern map, ported verbatim
  from internal/config/rules/rule_docs and internal/config/rules/
  system_rules.json. Adaptation: embedded as TypeScript constants.
- src/prompts.ts — the review and reflection prompt bodies (role,
  capabilities, focus rules, Ground A/B removal criteria, protected-subject
  vetoes), ported from internal/config/template/prompts. Adaptation: the
  upstream tool-call protocol (`code_comment` / `task_done` /
  `report_incorrect_comments`) is replaced by one structured JSON document.
- src/rules.ts — layered rule resolution and the system/user merge template
  ("## System-Specific Rules (Mandatory)" …), ported from
  internal/config/rules/system_rules.go. Adaptation: rewritten in
  TypeScript; the `include`/`exclude` filters are implemented against this
  plugin's exclusion list.
- src/pipeline.ts, src/bundle.ts, src/relocate.ts, src/git.ts — the review
  architecture (isolated per-bundle review units, file bundling heuristics,
  comment relocation, deterministic selection) reimplemented in TypeScript
  from the behavior described by the upstream documentation and delegate
  mode; no upstream Go source is compiled or transcribed.
- The model-facing guidance in src/index.ts is adapted from the upstream
  skills/open-code-review*/SKILL.md triage rubric.

Modifications are stated per file above and in the repository history.
